## The cold-gas thrusters' torque directions, transcribed from adcs-sim product.rs (fit_actuator_, rcs) and
## adcs-sim-core actuators.rs (Rcs::apply): six couples, a pair of thrusters firing together about each body axis, each
## way; a couple about axis k gives 2 F arm_k (F the part's thrust, arm_k its short arm about x and its long arm about y
## and z), the torque scaled by the duty each step. Since S7.11 also the arms about each axis, which adcs-sim product.rs
## (fit_actuator_, rcs) set out.
## The developer's transcription (S7.7; couple_arms S7.11), unsigned.
module rcstorque

## The most thruster couples a product carries.
const ACT_NC = 6

## The six couples' body torques [N m] at full thrust: +-2 F arm about x, y and z in turn.
fn couple_torques(thrust: real[N] in 0.001 .. 1, arm: real[m][3] in 0.01 .. 1) -> tau: real[N m][3][ACT_NC]
    tau = 0
    for ax in 0 .. 3
        tau[2*ax][ax] = 2.0*thrust*arm[ax]
        tau[2*ax + 1][ax] = -2.0*thrust*arm[ax]
    end
end

## The couples' arms [m] about x, y and z: the part's short arm about x, its long arm about y and about z.
fn couple_arms(arm_short: real[m] in 0.01 .. 1, arm_long: real[m] in 0.01 .. 1) -> arm: real[m][3]
    arm = [arm_short, arm_long, arm_long]
end
